  "description": "Today and Tomorrow is the fifth album as a leader by jazz pianist McCoy Tyner. It was recorded for the Impulse! label in 1963 and 1964. The two sessions featured trio performances by Tyner with bassist Jimmy Garrison and drummer Albert Heath and then sextet performances with tenor saxophonist John Gilmore, trumpeter Thad Jones, alto saxophonist Frank Strozier, bassist Butch Warren, and drummer Elvin Jones.",
